From 190a362e65caf15aa54d61ee8052bcd5cf2c8eb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: permissionBRICK <40219477+permissionBRICK@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:14:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(app): saving the settings keeps values the app has no
 field for

save_config wrote the form's config alone, so every key of config.yaml
the app does not know was dropped on save: settings of a newer helper,
of other tools, or added by hand. It now merges the form's values into
the file as it is at save time: each value the form has replaces the
file's, recursively through mappings, every other key stays. Lists are
the form's, whole. A file of an older schema (or none) is replaced as
before; one that does not parse, is not a mapping or is newer is an
error and never overwritten. The f32 thresholds keep their written form
(through text, not to_value, which widened 0.2 to 0.20000000298).

The app also knows the two face settings the helper gained:
detection.min_face_height (a face in front of the camera only) and
anti_spoofing.ir_recognition (the IR camera recognises too), with their
helper defaults (0, false) in defaults.yaml.
Tests: config (merge, older/newer/bad files, new fields), the golden
defaults.yaml and bindings.ts.
